==== GOLDEN ARTEFACT exit_read/cb702/out/exitpb_report_discovery.txt | bytes=23768 | sha256=8afb5f8891ae25c1a1ee63305f1ecb8dabe79563f9145c93f85c2a8905caecec | text
#702 EXIT READ - his partial and the stop after it, on discovery (2022-03-28..2024-12-31, DECIDES). Registered before any outcome: docs/analysis/cb_exit_partial_prereg_2026-10-19.md. Measurement only: nothing here switches the deciding comparison, the primary arm, the entry, the stop, a cell, a period, the horizon, the seed, the draw count, the n floor or the open-mark exclusion.
POPULATION: the pinned P5 fills (level tl, entry ORH5, the low-of-day stop no wider than one ADR20, the spec key's first break per base) - every arm walks the SAME fills, so the comparison is per trade; the pinned hourly-close fills (entry h60) are walked beside, descriptively. A group is the MATURE walks only; an open mark is counted, never in a number. ARMS: A = c3_p33_t20_cut3 (the control: the session-3 third whatever the price, stop to the fill after any third); pp = his RULING (the session-3 third only on a close above the fill, else skipped, the +2R leg stays armed; stop to the fill after a third); pp_wbe = the PRIMARY: pp + his PROPOSAL (after a third sold at p the stop rests at max(stop0, min(fill, fill - (p - fill)/2)), the whole-trade breakeven); beside: wbe (A's partial rule + the wbe stop), pp_s0 (pp with the stop left at stop0 after any third), pp5_wbe (the first close in sessions 3-5 above the fill, then the wbe stop). Common to all: 1/3; the +2R leg (day 0 on the minutes); the +1R-by-session-3 cut; the 20-day trail filled at the next open; R against the entry stop; horizon 120. The pp-family trail is live from session 3 whether or not the third sold.
INTERVAL RECIPE (the independent re-derivation reproduces it with no runner code): month-block bootstrap of the mean - blocks = the FILL month (E's month), 2,000 resamples of as many blocks as there are months, with replacement, each resample's mean = sum of the drawn blocks' values / their trade count; the 2.5 / 97.5 percentiles (numpy.percentile, linear); generator numpy.random.default_rng([702, zlib.crc32(key)]) with key 'exitpb|<period>|<entry>|<cell>|tl|<arm>' for a cell's R and 'exitpb_delta|<period>|<entry>|<cell>|tl|<x>-<y>' for a per-trade delta R(x) - R(y) (both walks mature); the stream is drawn as integers(0, n_months, size=(2000, n_months)). The deciding delta: pp_wbe - pp on C1, n floor 30; lower end > 0 = wbe WINS, upper end < 0 = wbe LOSES, else can't tell; C0 the same, read when C1 can't tell.
DATA CHECKS: freeze passed; module <SHA12:b/repo/agents/market_intelligence/consolidation_breakout.py|repo/agents/market_intelligence/consolidation_breakout.py>... equal; parity P1 / P2 4 fills, 0 mismatches; implementation checks passed; rows walked 4 x 6 arms

========== ENTRY orh5 / level tl - DECIDES ==========
EXPECTATIONS (fixed before the run; a missed one is reported first and changes NO rule):
  MET: C0 delta(pp_wbe - pp) point estimate +0.0000R on 1 trades (expected >= 0: it keeps runners the entry-price stop took out and costs only on trades that fall from the third to the original stop)
  MET: C1 median sessions held under pp_wbe 0 vs A's 0 (expected >=)
  MET: C0 median sessions held under pp_wbe 0 vs A's 0 (expected >=)

THE DECIDING EXIT BAR - per trade delta = R(pp_wbe) - R(pp) on the SAME fills (the ruled rule with vs without his stop); a trade with an open mark on either arm excluded and counted; 'n differing' = trades whose R differs at all
